---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import CachingSavingsCalculator from '../../components/CachingSavingsCalculator.jsx';
---
<ToolLayout title="Context Caching Savings Calculator" description="See how much prompt/context caching could save you when reusing the same large context across many requests.">
  <CachingSavingsCalculator client:load slot="tool" />

  <h2>Why context caching can meaningfully cut costs</h2>
  <p>If your application sends the same large system prompt, document, or few-shot examples on every request, you're paying full input-token price for that content every single time. Prompt/context caching lets providers charge a much lower rate for repeated context, since they've already processed it once.</p>

  <h2>How to use this calculator</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Enter the size of your repeated context (in tokens).</li>
    <li>Enter how many requests reuse that same context.</li>
    <li>Enter standard and cached pricing to see total savings.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Example</h2>
  <p>A 5,000-token system prompt reused across 1,000 requests/day, at $3/1M standard vs. $0.30/1M cached, saves the large majority of the input-token cost that would otherwise be paid repeatedly for identical content.</p>

  <h2>Common Context Caching Mistakes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Assuming caching applies automatically.</strong> Most providers require the cached portion to be identical and often need explicit API parameters or cache-eligible request structuring.</li>
    <li><strong>Caching content that changes on every request</strong> — caching only helps for genuinely repeated context, not dynamic per-request content.</li>
    <li><strong>Ignoring cache expiry windows</strong> — cached context typically expires after a period of inactivity, so very infrequent requests may not benefit.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When to Use This Caching Savings Calculator</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Estimating savings before implementing prompt caching in a high-volume app</li>
    <li>Justifying an engineering investment in restructuring prompts for cache eligibility</li>
    <li>Comparing cost impact of a large system prompt versus a smaller one</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Context Caching FAQ</h2>
  <p><strong>Does every AI provider support this?</strong> Major providers increasingly offer some form of prompt/context caching, but implementation details and pricing discounts vary — check your specific provider's documentation.</p>
</ToolLayout>
